EVALUATION.md §1, DECISIONS 331: W4001 counts the top-level values of the selected packages only.
`b.Gem` is broken: `a` selects two values typed by it, so the warning, at b's declaration, says
2 (b's own `local` value is not counted, b not being selected) and is shown with a's findings.
-- check-only --
-- project.canon --
project acme {
  canon: "0.1"
}
-- b/b.canon --
/// B.
package b

/// Gem.
record Gem {
  /// Weight.
  weight: Int

  check broken: weight < "5" else "broken"
}

/// Typed by Gem, in b.
let own: Gem = { weight: 1 }
-- a/a.canon --
/// A.
package a

import b

/// One.
let one: b.Gem = { weight: 1 }

/// Two.
let two: [b.Gem] = []
-- select --
a
-- findings.txt --
warning[W4001]  b/b.canon:5:8
  2 values were not evaluated or checked because b.Gem is broken: fix the errors in it or in the types it names

error[E3310]  b/b.canon:9:17
  < needs an orderable type, found String

1 error, 1 warning in 1 package (…)
